; ReIncarnation -- RIAPP Workbench frontend.
;
; WHY HERE AND NOT IN S:User-Startup: the startup-sequence runs User-Startup
; BEFORE Wanderer, so a GUI app launched from it has no Intuition to open a
; window on. Wanderer runs the scripts in SYS:WBStartup after the desktop is
; up, which is the first moment RIAPP can actually appear.
;
; The binary lives at SYS:Classes/ReIncarnation/RIAPP (next to Mods/ and
; Packs/) so it survives reboots; RAM: does not.
;
; ENV:ReIncarnation holds the persisted prefs (zoom mode, MIDI settings).
; ENVARC: is the archive the startup-sequence copies into ENV: at boot, so
; the guard below only matters on a first boot with no archive yet.

If NOT EXISTS "ENV:ReIncarnation"
    MakeDir "ENV:ReIncarnation"
EndIf

Run >NIL: SYS:Classes/ReIncarnation/RIAPP